# Jareb Content Hub

A modern content aggregation app that combines:

- News RSS feeds
- Programming and AI RSS sources
- YouTube developer videos
- GitHub trending repositories
- Search and category filtering
- User auth and favorites
- Supabase-ready favorites sync

## Features

- Aggregates multiple public sources
- Category filters: All, News, Programming, AI, Video, GitHub, Favorites
- Search by keyword, title, or source
- Mobile-friendly responsive layout
- Auth flow with email/password
- Favorites saved in localStorage and synchronised to Supabase if configured

## Stack

- Next.js
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- RSS Parser
- Supabase

## Getting started

1. Install dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

2. Create a local environment file

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

3. Fill in your Supabase values in `.env.local`

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
```

4. Run the development server

```bash
npm run dev
```

5. Open the app in your browser

```bash
http://localhost:3000
```

## Supabase setup

Create a `favorites` table in Supabase SQL editor:

```sql
create extension if not exists pgcrypto;

create table public.favorites (
  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  email text not null unique,
  item_ids jsonb not null default '[]'::jsonb,
  created_at timestamptz not null default now(),
  updated_at timestamptz not null default now()
);

alter table public.favorites enable row level security;

create policy "Anyone can insert their own favorites"
on public.favorites
for insert
with check (true);

create policy "Users can view their own favorites"
on public.favorites
for select
using (true);

create policy "Users can update their own favorites"
on public.favorites
for update
using (true)
with check (true);

create policy "Users can delete their own favorites"
on public.favorites
for delete
using (true);
```

## Notes

This version uses public RSS feeds and GitHub API endpoints. Some feeds may rate-limit or change format over time, but the app is designed to gracefully handle failures.
